From 9cf1f7e326b58f9f65d3be54899731afa0f40cc1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: executor <executor@nemo>
Date: Thu, 1 Oct 2026 09:50:46 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] parameters.in rewrite: lossless and idempotent
 (full-precision writer, list-directed reader)

NEMO rewrites parameters.in at start-up (write_parameters; original kept as .bak),
so a re-run in the same directory reads the rewritten file. Two latent hazards:
 - reals were written with es10.3e2 (4 significant digits): e.g. fixture_rung3
   a_max = 1.0001E-06 became 1.000E-06 (also dust_coag, ice_fiducial,
   ice_transport a_max guard digits). Results happened to be unchanged.
 - any key read but not written is silently dropped on rewrite (none today).

Changes (input_output.f90 only):
 - write_parameters: all 35 real writes es10.3e2 -> es24.16e3 (exact for a double).
 - read_parameters_in: all 51 numeric reads -> list-directed. Required, since
   (e12.6) reads 12 characters and would truncate full-precision values; also
   removes the Ew.d trap ('1000' read as 1e-3) and integer width limits.
   A blank numeric value now fails loudly instead of silently reading 0.
 - Round-trip contract documented at the top of both routines.

New guard tests/params_roundtrip.sh: static audit (reader keys subset of writer
keys, comment lines excluded), per-fixture value preservation, and re-run-in-place
idempotence (byte-identical abundances.out and second rewrite). Fails on the
unpatched code (4 fixtures), passes here; a planted dropped key is caught.

First-run outputs byte-identical to 352b51c (abundances, dust_distribution, rates)
on 7 configurations; roundtrip_derived.sh passes.
---
 src/input_output.f90      | 179 ++++++++++++++++++++------------------
 tests/params_roundtrip.sh |  83 ++++++++++++++++++
 2 files changed, 176 insertions(+), 86 deletions(-)
 create mode 100755 tests/params_roundtrip.sh

